# Living Survey: cancer                                                                                              
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Introduction                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **cancer**.                                               
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Recent Advances in Cancer Research                                                                                
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Recent literature has significantly expanded our understanding of cancer biology, diagnostics, and therapeutics      
through multi-omics, spatial transcriptomics, and metabolic interventions.                                           
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
**Pan-cancer & Multi-omics Atlases:** Recent releases of spatial transcriptomics datasets have provided foundational 
resources for studying metastatic brain tumors [^10.5281_zenodo.21816284] [^10.5281_zenodo.21816285]                 
[^10.5281_zenodo.21782885] [^10.5281_zenodo.21782884]. Concurrently, multi-omic prognostic modeling across over      
10,000 checkpoint blockade cases has elucidated tumor-immune ecosystem dynamics and identified prognostic cellular   
programs [^10.5281_zenodo.18706180] [^10.5281_zenodo.18706179]. Pan-cancer co-expression networks have further       
identified hub genes with potential for predicting drug responses [^10.5281_zenodo.2574643].                         
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
**Liquid Biopsy & Diagnostics:** Non-invasive diagnostics are advancing rapidly. Liquid biopsies leveraging cell-free
DNA (cfDNA) nucleosome positioning and repetitive element profiling have demonstrated high accuracy in discriminating
cancer patients from healthy controls across multiple cancer types [^10.5526_err-00042862] [^10.5526_err-00042900].  
Additionally, urinary proteomics has emerged as a viable approach for identifying breast cancer biomarkers           
[^10.5281_zenodo.20393677].                                                                                          
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
**Metabolic & Nutritional Interventions:** Metabolic plasticity remains a critical therapeutic vulnerability. Fasting
and polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFAs) have been shown to induce ferroptosis and lipid peroxidation in breast cancer
cells by modulating mitochondrial ROS production [^10.21954_ou.ro.00108036]. Similarly, omega-3 fatty acids (EPA)    
disrupt mitochondrial succinylation networks, inhibiting prostate cancer growth through aspartate biosynthesis       
depletion and ferroptosis induction [^10.17638_03195029].                                                            
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
**Oncogenic Mechanisms & Signaling:** Research continues to unravel critical signaling pathways driving malignancy.  
Deubiquitinating enzymes (DUBs) regulating YAP/TAZ activity were identified in mesothelioma and head and neck        
cancers, with USP42 highlighted as a potential therapeutic target [^10.17638_03193849]. The DEK oncoprotein's        
phosphorylation-dependent chromatin remodeling role in metastatic melanoma was also characterized, linking it to     
transcriptional repression and chromatin compaction [^10.17638_03194520]. Furthermore, clear cell renal cell         
carcinoma (ccRCC) lung metastases were found to harbor cancer-associated fibroblast lymphocyte exclusion sites that  
form confined tumor microenvironments [^10.5281_zenodo.18767278] [^10.5281_zenodo.18767279].                         
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
**Drug Discovery & Epidemiology:** Novel non-genotoxic topoisomerase II catalytic inhibitors for cancer therapy have 
been developed [^10.14288_1.0451818]. Transcriptomic analysis of colorectal cancer in Korean cohorts revealed        
distinct molecular subtypes and potential therapeutic targets [^10.5281_zenodo.8307739]. Finally, environmental      
factors, specifically the built environment, have been linked to cancer risk, emphasizing the role of external       
influences in oncogenesis [^10.14288_1.0451801].                                                                     
                                                                                                                     

